<title>BELGIUM: Soros says markets calm on delayed Italian EMU entry.</title>
<headline>Soros says markets calm on delayed Italian EMU entry.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financier George Soros said on Thursday that financial markets would react calmly to the prospect of a delayed Italian entry into European monetary union, and suggested it was likely.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the markets would take it very calmly. It's more or less in the cards,&quot; he told Reuters before a meeting with European Commission President Jacques Santer.</p>
<p>Asked about news reports on Wednesday suggesting that European monetary officials were considering a compromise plan to delay Italy's entry, Soros said: &quot;I smelt that.&quot;</p>
<p>EU officials said Soros was visiting Santer to discuss a European charter for EU citizens.</p>
</text>
